:: Fishing Pier Ask Whitney To Stay
<<effects>>
<<set $daily.fishing.pier.whitney.phase to "alone">>

<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
	"Could you... stay? Just you."
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"Send them home. Stay."
<<else>>
	"Tell them to go. Stay with me."
<</if>>
<br><br>

Whitney looks at you for a moment. Then <<nnpc_he "Whitney">> tips <<nnpc_his "Whitney">> chin at <<nnpc_his "Whitney">> friends. "You heard. Get out."
<br><br>

There are a few grumbled complaints, but they collect their things and head off along the pier without much argument. Whitney watches until they're gone, then settles back against the railing beside you, picking up <<nnpc_his "Whitney">> cider.
<br><br>

<<link [[Return to Fishing|Fishing Pier Wait]]>><</link>>


:: Fishing Pier Whitney Alone Move Close
<<effects>>
You shift your weight, moving closer to Whitney until you're standing side by side.  You nestle yourself against <<nnpc_him "Whitney">>, your shoulder pressing against <<nnpc_his "Whitney">> arm. For a moment, <<nnpc_he "Whitney">> stays still. Then, without looking at you, <<nnpc_he "Whitney">> raises <<nnpc_his "Whitney">> arm and wraps it around you, pulling you close, pressing you firmly against <<nnpc_his "Whitney">> side.
<br><br>

You rest your head just below <<nnpc_his "Whitney">> shoulder, nestled against <<nnpc_his "Whitney">> chest. The sound of <<nnpc_his "Whitney">> heartbeat is steady and calm. <<nnpc_He "Whitney">> doesn't say anything, just keeps <<nnpc_his "Whitney">> arm around you.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Fishing Pier Wait]]>><</link>>


